@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification] mila-transport-hegel-properties
Hegel properties MUST cover host certificate blob and line parsing and trust
document decoding as total over arbitrary bytes, `reconcile_trust` authority
preservation, latest retirement and idempotence, `WatchRequest` dedup and
filter bounds, `TerminalAttachRequest` dimension bounds, `decode_watch_line`
totality, its byte cap and exact decoding of generated events, and the PTY
policy's refusal of stale generations and closed sessions against an
independent state model. Certificate verification, certificate-only key
exchange, external device signing and PTY channel behaviour stay with the
real-TCP russh tests and the shared Elixir certificate fixtures.
